{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Lavan the son of Nahor.</b> It should have said 'Lavan the son of Bethuel,' but grandchildren are considered like children; and similar is ״אחותי בת אבי״, whose meaning is 'the daughter of my father's son,' for she was the daughter of Haran, his [Terah's] son. Or he calls him 'the son of Nahor' because Nahor, the brother of Abraham, was a man of the Name and of prominence, and Lavan was not known in the land by the name of Bethuel his father, for he was an inferior man, and therefore he needed to say 'the son of Nahor':"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "The word הכ׳ appears to be an abbreviation for הכתוב (\"the verse\"); resolved by context."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:04.074761256Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}